@startuml deployment

' Three topologies for the same app. Verified against docker-compose.yml and
' how-to/deploy-and-host.md. Local + Forge verified 2026-09-07; the Railway
' package redrawn 2026-09-12 for ADR-0024 (Railpack, not the custom Dockerfile
' ADR-0023 first described — that image failed eleven straight deploys, see
' troubleshooting/infra-and-environment.md). Local package re-verified
' 2026-09-13 against the current docker-compose.yml: a `queue` service
' (php artisan queue:work) now runs locally too, added when
' QUEUE_CONNECTION moved off `sync` for the newsletter double-opt-in flow —
' it was missing from this diagram until now.
' Railway package redrawn again 2026-09-14 for ADR-0025 (split seed/upload
' media disks): a volume is now mounted on the real web service at
' /app/storage/app/media, confirmed against the live box (app root is /app,
' NOT /var/www/html — ADR-0023's original path was stale, see ADR-0025).
' RailwayWorker/RailwayCron remain PLANNED, not yet created — same caveat
' this diagram already carried before this revision, unchanged here.
' The gap between Local and Forge is the whole point of deploy-and-host.md's
' checklist — anything fixed only in docker/nginx/*.conf reaches neither
' deployed box. Railway has no such gap: Railpack builds its own image, so
' this repo's docker/nginx/*.conf was never relevant to it in the first place.
'
' NOTE: the .svg/.pdf beside this file are STALE relative to this source.
' Regenerate with the commands in docs/reference/diagrams/README.md — there
' is no render script in this repo and nothing regenerates them automatically.

title Local Docker vs. Railway (beta, actual) vs. Forge (ADR-0001, never built)

package "Local development — docker-compose.yml" {
  node "webserver\nnginx:1.27-alpine" as LocalNginx
  node "app\n(PHP-FPM, built from\ndocker/php/Dockerfile)" as LocalApp
  node "db\nmysql:8.0\n(durability RELAXED —\nlocal only, see\ntroubleshooting/database-and-migrations.md)" as LocalDB
  node "vite\nnode:22-alpine\n(HMR dev server)" as LocalVite
  node "mailpit\n(catches outbound mail,\nweb UI on :8025)" as LocalMail
  node "queue\n(PHP-FPM, same image,\nphp artisan queue:work)" as LocalQueue

  LocalNginx --> LocalApp : fastcgi :9000
  LocalApp --> LocalDB : :3306
  LocalApp --> LocalMail : SMTP :1025
  LocalNginx ..> LocalVite : dev asset\nproxy (HMR)
  LocalQueue --> LocalDB : :3306

  note bottom of LocalQueue
    QUEUE_CONNECTION=database.
    Nothing runs schedule:run
    locally — orders:expire-unpaid
    and carts:expire need a manual
    `artisan schedule:run` or a
    cron loop; Forge/Railway handle
    this in their own deploy target.
  end note

  note bottom of LocalDB
    innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=2,
    sync_binlog=0, --skip-log-bin.
    Traded for speed — see the
    "Migrations and tests are
    unbearably slow" troubleshooting
    entry for why this exists.
  end note
}

package "Beta — Railway (ADR-0023 platform, ADR-0024 build, ADR-0025 media)" {
  node "web service\nRailpack: FrankenPHP + Caddy\nRoot Directory: src\napp root: /app (NOT /var/www/html)" as RailwayWeb
  node "worker service\nqueue:work\n(same repo, same Root Dir)" as RailwayWorker
  node "scheduler service\nschedule:work\n(same repo, same Root Dir)" as RailwayCron
  database "MySQL\n(Railway-managed)" as RailwayDB
  storage "media volume\nmounted at\n/app/storage/app/media" as RailwayVolume

  cloud "Railway edge + proxy\nTLS terminates HERE\nreaches the container over IPv6" as RailwayEdge

  RailwayEdge --> RailwayWeb : plain HTTP\n+ X-Forwarded-*\nCaddy binds $PORT on\nall interfaces itself
  RailwayWeb --> RailwayDB
  RailwayWorker --> RailwayDB
  RailwayCron --> RailwayDB
  RailwayWeb --> RailwayVolume : admin uploads only\n(MEDIA_DISK=media)

  note bottom of RailwayEdge
    <b>trustProxies(at: '*') in bootstrap/app.php</b>
    is what makes isSecure() true past this point.
    Without it: http:// links, broken image URLs
    (the public disk builds them from APP_URL),
    and a Secure cookie the framework thinks
    it cannot send. ADR-0023.
  end note

  note bottom of RailwayCron
    orders:expire-unpaid runs here, every minute,
    via schedule:work. ADR-0022's stock release
    depends on it, and reliability here is
    UNVERIFIED — check on the box, do not assume.
  end note

  note bottom of RailwayWeb
    No Dockerfile: Railpack detects Laravel from
    artisan and builds FrankenPHP/Caddy itself.
    RAILPACK_SKIP_MIGRATIONS=true — migrate runs
    in preDeployCommand instead, with
    --schema-path=/nonexistent (no mysql client
    in this image; migrations replay over PDO).
    Seed via `railway ssh`, never `railway run`
    (which executes on the operator's own
    machine and cannot reach *.railway.internal).
    APP_ENV=demo, never production — three
    seeders refuse when it is 'production'.
  end note

  note bottom of RailwayVolume
    ADR-0025. Seeded demo images stay OUT of
    here — they ship inside the image at
    storage/app/public/demo/, on the 'public'
    disk, and survive a redeploy by being IN
    the container. Only admin-uploaded media
    (ProductImage::uploadDisk(), 'articles'/
    'product-images' prefixes) lands on this
    volume, which is what makes an uploaded
    image survive a redeploy for the first time.
    MEDIA_DISK=public is the one-variable
    rollback if this volume misbehaves.
  end note
}

package "Production — Laravel Forge (ADR-0001, never provisioned)" {
  node "VPS" {
    node "nginx\n(Forge-provisioned,\nNOT this repo's\ndocker/nginx/*.conf)" as ProdNginx
    node "PHP-FPM\n(Forge-provisioned)" as ProdApp
  }
  database "MySQL\n(Forge-provisioned,\nDEFAULT durability —\nnothing relaxed)" as ProdDB

  ProdNginx --> ProdApp : fastcgi
  ProdApp --> ProdDB

  note bottom of ProdNginx
    No containers here at all.
    Owed independently, per
    how-to/deploy-and-host.md:
    * X-Content-Type-Options header (SEC-007)
    * server_tokens off / expose_php Off (SEC-004)
    * Stripe webhook IP allowlist
    * SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true
  end note
}

LocalNginx -[hidden]right-> RailwayWeb
RailwayWeb -[hidden]right-> ProdNginx

note as Gap
  <b>The Local/Forge gap is why deploy-and-host.md's checklist exists</b>
  for THAT pairing — anything fixed only in this repo's
  docker/nginx/*.conf, or only in the local .env, is invisible
  to a Forge VPS and has to be set again, deliberately, there.

  Railway has no equivalent gap: Railpack builds its own image,
  so docker/nginx/*.conf was never relevant to it — a different
  reason the same file cannot be assumed to cover Railway too.

  As of this diagram, Railway deploys have not yet succeeded;
  Forge has never been provisioned at all. Local is the only
  topology actually verified running end to end.
end note

Gap .. LocalNginx
Gap .. RailwayWeb
Gap .. ProdNginx

@enduml
